======================================================================
STEP 5: combine (a)+(b)+(c) -- exact closure, upper bound
======================================================================
a(n) := max_x h(n,x) is continuous on real n>2 (max of a jointly
continuous function over the compact set x in [0,1]).
For n>3 (hence for all integer n>=5): a(n) never equals M3, because
  - boundary x=0: h(n,0)=0 != M3 (M3>0);
  - boundary x=1: h(n,1)=6/[(n-1)(n-2)] < M3 for n>n0_boundary(<5);
  - interior: STEP 4 rules out any interior critical value = M3 for
    real n>~2.17.
Since a(n) is continuous, never equal to M3 on (n0_boundary,infinity),
and a(6) < M3 (checked below, exact), by the Intermediate Value
Theorem a(n) < M3 for ALL real n > n0_boundary, in particular for
every integer n>=5.
a(6) = max_x h(6,x) = 0.4520877254732390178230291  at x* = 0.371155841697152
a(6) < M3  CONFIRMED (exact).

